---
import PlainSummary from '../PlainSummary.astro';
---
<section class="sec" id="module-02" aria-labelledby="m2-h" data-depth="0.37">
  <div class="wrap mod__grid">
    <div class="col">
      <p class="eyebrow">MODULE 02 · FIELD READINESS</p>
      <h2 class="h2 recede-h" id="m2-h">Take the archive into the field.</h2>
      <p class="narr recede">Signal is not guaranteed where you’re going. Install Deepwell like an app, save the files you’ll need, and go. Tunnel, plane, a site with no reception: the archive comes with you, and it remembers exactly where you stopped.</p>
      <ul class="feat">
        <li><strong>Truly offline.</strong> Save articles and read them with no connection at all.</li>
        <li><strong>Never lose your place.</strong> Deepwell resumes at the exact paragraph, every time.</li>
        <li><strong>Your library.</strong> Keep the files you love close, organized the way you like.</li>
      </ul>
      <PlainSummary>Install it, save articles, read with no internet. It remembers your place.</PlainSummary>
    </div>
    <div class="mod__visual mod__visual--low">
      <figure class="reader reader--sm" aria-label="Offline reading: saved for field use, resuming at the exact paragraph">
        <i class="reader__lamp" aria-hidden="true" style="opacity: 0.7"></i>
        <i class="reader__edge" aria-hidden="true" style="opacity: 0.7"></i>
        <div class="reader__meta"><span><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v12"></path><path d="m7 10 5 5 5-5"></path><path d="M5 21h14"></path></svg>Deepwell sync — secured for field use</span></div>
        <div class="reader__prog" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></div>
        <div class="reader__body">
          <div class="reader__para"><span class="reader__mark">¶ 14</span><p>By the fourth floor the drawers had stopped agreeing with the index. There were more of them than the plans allowed for, and they ran further back than the walls. The clerk counted anyway. That was the job.</p></div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
